# Line endings. This file is a SUPERSET of the game branch's .gitattributes (which pins only
# .luau / .json / .md), so copying it over the game branch's copy changes nothing there.
#
# Why: with Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true, files without a rule are checked out
# with CRLF endings. A CRLF bash script dies immediately in Git Bash ("$'\r': command not found"),
# so the bash scripts and the tool config files are pinned to LF. Rojo round-trips Luau/JSON
# byte-for-byte when they are LF. PowerShell is happiest with CRLF.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.luau      text eol=lf
*.lua       text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
.luaurc     text eol=lf
lint/*.txt  text eol=lf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
